{{!
  Use-case input: what the adapter hands the use case (from the request DTO, the path, the caller).
  validate() covers presence only; business rules live in the domain.
  Exemplars: therapeutic-relation-usecase .../exclusion/usecase/CreateTherapeuticExclusionRequest.java,
             .../DeleteTherapeuticExclusionRequest.java (validate())
  Target: <capability>-usecase/src/main/java/<pkg>/<Request>Request.java
  Package: "package" is the full package of the file (no suffix is appended).
  Vars:   package, Request (class name without "Request", e.g. CreateGadget), imports[],
          fields[type, name, notBlank, primitive]
  Left to you: nothing for a plain input; drop validate() when the domain validates everything.
}}
